  This is the polynomial remainder theorem.        https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polynomial_remainder_theorem
  It basically says that instead of bothering with polynomial long division, when the divisor is of order 1, you can get the remainder by using
  the last (zeroth-order) coefficient of the divisor as the dividend's variable.
  The divisor must be normalised by factoring out its leading coefficient:

    a x + b  <--  a (x + b/a)    then the remainder is  R [N-1]  =  P [N] (b/a)

